# Project conventions

## Structure

```
src/
├── lib/          # Pure logic, no React: notation, sheet model, geometry, view, export
├── components/   # React components; Board.tsx is the one SVG renderer for screen, print, export
├── App.tsx       # Sheet state, persistence, layout
└── styles.css    # All styles: tokens on :root, dark mode, print rules
e2e/              # Playwright specs
public/engine/    # Vendored Stockfish (lite, single-threaded WASM) and its licence
```

- Relative imports, no path aliases, no barrel files.
- New logic goes in `src/lib/<thing>.ts` with `src/lib/<thing>.test.ts` beside it.

## Patterns

- State is one `Sheet` object in `App`, in memory only. Diagrams are updated with
  `Partial<Diagram>` patches. Tests pass a starting sheet with `<App initialSheet={...} />`.
- Derive positions with `diagramView(diagram)`; never store FENs derived from notation.
- Styling: CSS custom properties in `styles.css`. Board and print colours are fixed (they
  must look the same on paper in both themes); everything else uses tokens.
- Print layout uses mm units and lives in the `.page` rules; check `test-results/screens`.

## Testing

- Logic: Vitest unit tests next to the module.
- UI behaviour: Testing Library tests in `src/App.test.tsx`, seeding the sheet via `initialSheet`.
- Pointer interaction, print and layout: Playwright in `e2e/`, because jsdom has no layout.
- A new feature needs a unit or component test; UI changes also need a look at screenshots.
